PR 26 integration review fixes on the renderer paths that run by default.
1) Vertex ring (patches 59/67/68, zzz-001): four segments with one fence each instead of one fence per lap.
   Leaving a segment fences the draws that read it; entering one waits on the fence taken three segments
   earlier, so a wrap normally waits for nothing. zzz-001 was correct but fenced the lap being left and waited
   on it at once: a full CPU/GPU drain every 32 MB, i.e. a periodic hitch on slow GPUs. Chunks never straddle a
   segment; a chunk larger than one segment (8 MB; the largest batch measured is 84 KB) takes the callers'
   existing spill buffers. Only the persistent map is fenced: BufferSubData is ordered by the driver. Timeout,
   WAIT_FAILED and a null fence still fall back to glFinish, never to an unconfirmed overwrite.
2) Op::Run encoder (patch 66): the zero tail of a primitive with fewer than three vertices was read from one
   GSVertex as if it were three (stack over-read for points and empty primitives, ASan in
   render-delivery-tests submit_run/0, /1, /255), and `base += kGsRunMaxPrims` in the loop header could wrap
   at UINT32_MAX. Both were already fixed in fix-chore's patch 66; restored here on top of the PR chain.
3) glBufferStorage on a 4.3 context is kept only when the driver lists ARB_buffer_storage (a non-null entry
   point is not support on every Windows driver); otherwise the ring uses BufferSubData. One stderr line says
   which path a session took.
4) Queue record guard (patch 89): Op::Vertices required sizeof(GSPrimitiveBatch), but the compact encoder writes
   only offsetof(GSPrimitiveBatch, state) (the state travels in its own DrawState record). Every primitive
   submitted outside a run with PS2X_GS_COMPACT_QUEUE on (the default) was dropped as "record payload
   truncated", i.e. PS2X_GS_RUN=0 drew nothing through the threaded backend. gow_gs_run_tests caught it.
5) PS2X_GS_RUN is read per GS again (patch 66 had made it a function static, read once per process), as in
   fix-chore. No runtime cost difference: the constructor runs once per session.
Validation: tools/test/render-delivery-tests.py (extracted production bodies, mock GL, ASan): 12/12;
gow_gs_run_tests (production frontend + threaded queue, run on/off, compact on/off): pass.
No FPS claim; the GPU-side effect needs the laptop A/B in docs/research/pr26-integration.md.
